      "headline": "The Class Reunion: Same Faces, Brand New Weather",
      "keyInsight": "We love to believe that once we build a comfortable life, the ground underneath us stops shaking. But look around any table of old friends. Everyone brought the same old habits into completely unexpected storms. One person lost a business to sudden technology shifts. Another felt trapped in a job that slowly lost its spark. The funny paradox is that we all pretend surprise when life rearrenges the furniture. Change is not an uninvited party crasher. Change is the room itself, quietly remodeling while you sleep. The people who suffer most are never the ones who faced tough breaks. They are the ones who waited for yesterday to return on a silver platter. They treated a temporary season like a permanent house. When you view your current routine as an unmovable statue, even a gentle breeze feels like an earthquake. The real shocker at the reunion was not how much the world had shifted. It was how stubbornly everyone tried to drive forward while staring only into their rearview mirror.",
